            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">Inventory for a high pressure storage Type I tank, with a capacity of 35 kg of hydrogen at 200 bar. Rough approximation: based on Jumbo cylinder model from Sino Energy Tech. A 2â€™420 kg heavy steel tank for a volume of 2â€™320 liters, for storing hydrogen at a pressure of 200 bar, equivalent to 35 kg of hydrogen stored at 15 degrees Celsius. The dataset "storage production, 10'000 l" is used as a proxy, and only the inputs of steel, steel working and transport inputs have been modified accordingly. A lifetime of 20 years is assumed. For more information, refer to Sacchi and Bauer, 2023.

